+# Outcome Metrics
+
+Status: approved
+Slug: outcome-metrics
+
+## Roles
+- implementer: builds the change described here
+- reviewer: checks the change against this spec
+- qa: checks the scenarios below with tests
+- product_owner: owns the purpose and accepts the result
+
+## Purpose
+A run report says how one attempt went. Nothing said how the line performs: how often work is approved without being sent back, how often each reviewer objects, how often the checks gate stops work before review, what an approved work order costs. This spec computes those figures from the run reports already on record, without running anything again.
+
+## Requirements
+- outcome_metrics takes the run reports of a project, the current report of each work order and every archived earlier run, and returns the figures under the schema anvil/outcomes@1.
+- A judged run is one whose verdict is approved, rejected or changes_requested. Approval rate, first pass approval rate (approved with no loopback) and loopbacks per judged run are computed over judged runs only.
+- Gate failure rate is the share of runs where the checks gate ran (passed or failed) in which it failed. A gate that was not configured did not run.
+- For each reviewer, the objection rate is the share of its counted reviews whose verdict was not pass.
+- Tokens per approved work order divides every token on record, failed and earlier runs included, by the number of work orders with an approved run.
+- A figure with nothing to measure is None, never zero. Runs are also counted by run state, and budget stopped runs and write authority violations are counted.
+- The status page shows an Outcomes panel for a project with at least one run, and status/usage.json carries the figures under outcomes. anvil metrics <project> prints them as JSON.
+- Limit, stated plainly: the figures describe the runs on record. A repository that keeps only its approved runs will read 100 percent.
+
+## Scenarios
+
+### Scenario: Rates are computed over judged runs
+- S1: Given reports with approved, sent back, rejected, packet only and aborted runs, when the metrics are computed, then approval, first pass approval and loopbacks per run count only the runs that reached an approver verdict, and runs are counted by state.
+
+### Scenario: Nothing measured is None
+- S2: Given reports with no judged run, no gate run and no agent call, when the metrics are computed, then every rate and the token figures are None.
+
+### Scenario: Objection rate per reviewer
+- S3: Given reports whose approver counted reviews, when the metrics are computed, then each reviewer has its number of counted reviews, its objections and their ratio.
+
+### Scenario: The status page and usage file carry the outcomes
+- S4: Given a project with recorded runs, when the status page is generated, then the page has an Outcomes panel and usage.json has the outcomes; and given a project with no runs, then the page has no Outcomes panel.
+
+### Scenario: The CLI prints the metrics
+- S5: Given a project with recorded runs, when anvil metrics runs, then it prints the figures as JSON and exits zero.
+
+### Scenario: Tokens per approved work order counts every run
+- S6: Given a work order approved on its second run and another that was rejected, when the metrics are computed, then the tokens of all three runs are divided by the one approved work order.
